    ('What does enum.ReprEnum() do?', '`enum.ReprEnum()`: Only changes the repr(), leaving str() and format() to the mixed-in type.'),
    ('What does enum.StrEnum() do?', '`enum.StrEnum()`: Enum where members are also (and must be) strings'),
    ('What does enum.auto() do?', '`enum.auto()`: Instances are replaced with an appropriate value in Enum class suites.'),
    ('What does enum.bin() do?', '`enum.bin()`: Like built-in bin(), except negative values are represented in twos-compliment, and the leading bit always indicates sign (0=positive, 1=negative).'),
    ('What does enum.global_enum() do?', "`enum.global_enum()`: decorator that makes the repr() of an enum member reference its module instead of its class; also exports all members to the enum's module's global namespace"),
